From 5b562bcbae154e566b59fa98bb61be9965e4d20e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ravindra Lakkireddy <85186928+rlakki08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 17:56:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat: measure and replace by voice (remove_component,
 restore_component, measure_cavity, place_part, switching)

The AirTools app's e2e hand-off (docs/handoff/p4-e2e): on the fast path (no LLM),
from the loaded site's parts.r<rev>.json and the headset's removed/cavity context:
- "remove / take out the dishwasher" -> remove_component {component_id}, the gap's size said
- "measure it / the gap" -> measure_cavity {component_id} (the headset tapes it)
- "find a dishwasher that fits" -> find_part with SearchRequest.cavity: every candidate's
  fit is against the gap's three axes, fitting ones first
- "put it in there" -> place_part {part_id, model_url, component_id, fits, clearance_mm, cycle}
  for the first candidate that fits (else the least over)
- "next / previous one", "show me option 2" -> place_part for that candidate
- "put it back" -> restore_component
Up to four joined by and / then / commas in one reply. A running coach keeps next/back and
a reimagine keeps remove/swap. server/replace.py (phrases, parts file, 3-axis fit),
tests/test_replace.py, docs/api.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
